# Comprehensive Example: Defined Terms + Article Semantics

# Define terms for better LLM expansion
liability_cap - the highest amount the liability settlement can go
termination_notice - the number of days required before contract termination
Effective Date - the date when the contract becomes binding
Maximum Liability - the total cap on all liability claims combined

Load document

# Article semantics in action:

# "a/an" = introducing/defining (existential - any instance satisfies)
Document must contain a Liability Clause
Document must contain an Indemnification Clause
Document must contain a Termination Clause

# "the" = referencing specific instance (definite)
the Document must contain the Effective Date
the Document must contain the Maximum Liability

# "All" = universal quantifier (every instance must satisfy)
All Documents must contain a Confidentiality Clause

# Extract using defined terms
# Parser expands definitions for better matching
Find liability_cap and save as liability_cap
Find termination_notice and save as termination_notice
Find Maximum Liability and save as maximum_liability

# Validations
liability_cap must be at least 1000000
termination_notice must be at least 30
maximum_liability must be at least 5000000
